    "reading": "the folded kernel K = 2 sin(th)/(cos phi - cos th) has the far-field decay built in (sin th -> 0), and its principal value over (0, pi) is exactly zero -- it is the conjugate of the constant function -- so the p.v. can be handled by a GLOBAL subtraction with no band, no matching scale and no remainder term.  v6 needed all three, and each cost a crude constant."
