    "reading": "every rho gives a VALID bound; the choice is a free parameter of the estimate, not an approximation.  The neutral rule rho = 1 -- v8's default, and the natural one -- is WORSE than the crude bound it replaces, because in the closure T is ~10x S and the neutral rule charges the expensive account.  Different consumers want different rho: the closure feeds a large T, C_Q maximises over the unit simplex where the ratio is O(1)."
